# What this corpus draws no page for. One entry per line -- a basename
# for a program that produces no page at all, a basename and " pN" for
# one page of a program that produces others -- each with the reason it
# draws nothing.
#
# A program that draws nothing because it is a fragment, or a procedure
# set another program reads, is not a defect; one that draws nothing
# because this interpreter refused it is. The reason is what tells them
# apart, which is why an entry without one is not an entry.
